{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"Tracker.Records","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Records","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"externalID":"s:8Trackers7TrackerV7RecordsV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Records","kind":"identifier"}],"extendedModule":"Trackers","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Trackers\/Records.swift#L28","fileName":"Records.swift"}},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sequence ends once the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/finish()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is called, or its every copy is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"released, and every record before it has been read. Records tracked while nothing is reading wait in memory, without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound, for the next read, so none tracked before a delivery starts, or between two, is lost.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A read whose task is cancelled returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and takes nothing: the next read gets the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record it was waiting for, and every one after. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/noOp","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" tracker’s records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One task reads at a time. The first iterator to read holds the records until its iteration","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends or the iterator is released, as it is when its task ends. An iterator that reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"meanwhile waits its turn, logging a warning as it starts to, then reads on from the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record; several wait in the order they came, and one whose task is cancelled while it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"waits returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So a delivery started right after a cancelled one has stopped, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while it is stopping, delivers every record the cancelled one didn’t read.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/Sci"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncIterator"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/makeAsyncIterator()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"identifiers":[